Note on content licensing, which this licence does NOT cover:

- The bundled Bhagavad Gita Sanskrit and its English translation (Swami
  Sivananda) come from the Unlicense `gita/gita` dataset and are public domain.
- The Hindi translation (Swami Ramsukhdas) is NOT public domain and is included
  for personal use only; it must be removed or replaced before any
  redistribution beyond personal use.
- The classical Sanskrit texts described in the Shastra library are public
  domain, but their modern translations and commentaries are not, and none of
  their text is reproduced here.
- Cheiro (d. 1936) and Benham (1900) are public domain, and are the sources for
  the numerology and palmistry reference material.
- Lal Kitab (Pt. Roop Chand Joshi, d. 1982) is described, never reproduced.
